A||||2||Johnson's85SE||Steering diagnosis||||5||
Z||000000||Johnson's85SE||01-29-2001||04:08 PM||||Hi,<BR>  It is suspension time on my SE. 204,000KMs. I know I need new front shocks, but the steering dampener might be going. I heared on here that if your car is really drifty on rough road, that the steering dampeneer might be suspect. If i change the dampener and the front shocks, will I need a wheel alignment? I know I should get one, but I am fed up with the constant repairs. *** New engine, New Clutch, tons of minor things.*** Thanks, Chris from Calgary  <BR><P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ed||01-29-2001||04:25 PM||||Bad shocks would make it bounce around.  I suppose you've checked them by looking for fluid streaks down the sides, or by pushing on the fender and seeing the car only bounce once or twice?<P>A bad steering damper will show itself by you're having a lot of kick back through the steering wheel.  It wouldn't cause your car to drift, although the steering would be "easier".  In fact, some folks would take off the damper for that reason.  I kept mine on my car.<P>Neither of these would require you to get an alignment, although if you replace the rear struts you would.  <P>Drift could be due to a lot of things, including something as simple as over inflated front tires or even oversized tires, but drift could also be caused by something serious such as the front suspension bushings giving out.  <P>If you know the shocks are bad, certainly replace those.  Check tire pressure. Then go to a mechanic.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Johnson's85SE||01-29-2001||05:29 PM||||Thanks, for the info ED. <BR> <BR>Thanks,<BR>  Chris<BR>||||reg||12
